pocket-motion-only: extends 0019's gradient paint (PAINT_PUSH, ops 69/70), which only this rasteriser draws.

0029 — a radial gradient takes the ending shape it names.

0019's radial was CSS's default and nothing else: the farthest-corner
ellipse about the box centre. On a wide box a "glow" was a flat oval, and a
round one had to be a square box around a circle. `bg-radial-circle` is
the farthest-corner circle; `bg-radial-[<shape>_<size>]` and
`bg-[radial-gradient(<shape> <size>, …)]` take CSS's shape (`circle`,
`ellipse`) and size (`closest-side`, `farthest-side`, `closest-corner`,
`farthest-corner`), each optional, either order. About the box centre the
closest and farthest corner are one point and an ellipse's closest and
farthest side are one size, so five shapes cover every pair: the ellipse
(default) and the circle to the farthest corner, the ellipse to the sides,
and the circle to the closest or farthest side. A length, a percentage or
`at <position>` is refused, not dropped to the default. Stop positions and
colours animate as before; the shape is an enum and does not.

What it adds: PROP `gradShape` = 184 (enum `GradShape { Ellipse: 0,
Circle: 1, EllipseClosestSide: 2, CircleClosestSide: 3, CircleFarthestSide:
4 }`); `Resolved.grad_shape`; `emit_paint_push` picks the radii, so the
rasteriser and PAINT_PUSH's format are unchanged; the compiler declares the
shape only when it is not the default ellipse, so every literal that
compiled before compiles to the same record.

Guard: `a_radial_gradient_takes_the_ending_shape_it_names`
(`engine/core/src/tests.rs`): white-to-black on a 200 x 40 box, read 15 px
right of the centre and 15 px below it; each shape matches its radii within
2 levels, and the circles read the same on both axes while the ellipses do
not. Red with the shape ignored (Circle reads 227 where its radius gives
216), green with it. `tests/tailwind.test.ts` pins the compiler.

Ledgers, against the same tree without this patch: no digest and no
`visibility` row moves — `compositions/gradients` draws the default
ellipse, whose radii and style record are the ones it had.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

